00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Thank you.

33
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:32,100
What's the deal with you, kid? Are you physically incapable of not fighting something? For some kind of disorder?

34
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:35,060
My body just moved on its own! Really?

35
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:39,060
Come on. You were beat up already and you fought anyway.

36
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:42,380
You're getting checked out. That head needs looking at.

37
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,580
Well, yeah, now it does, thanks to you!

38
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:47,800
Hey, come on in, Yami. Brought someone to see me?

39
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,420
Who's that guy?

40
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:56,940
He's a lot less impressive looking than this fancy tower. But don't let that fool you. This guy's actually the kingdom's best quack.

41
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,020
You're so mean.

42
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:05,260
He's a real powerful recovery mage who's done a pretty decent job keeping my arms attached to my body. So I figured he could take a look at yours.

43
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:08,840
That isn't helping, sir!

44
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:16,240
Nice to meet you. The name's Owen, and I report directly to the Wizard King himself. How can I help?

45
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:19,280
Yes, sir! I'm Asta! Nice to meet you, too!

46
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:23,600
Of course. I've heard all about you. Yami gets chatty when he's drinking.

47
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:24,840
What did he say?

48
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:31,280
Well, he's told a few stories about how your sword can nullify magic. Who knew something like that was even possible?

49
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:37,780
This guy reports directly to the Wizard King? It doesn't take a genius to figure out he must be seriously awesome!

50
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:45,560
Well, I gotta see a man about a dog, so... I'm gonna win today. I can feel it in my bones.

51
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:48,680
Got some gambling to do? Good luck, sir!

52
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:53,440
You know, that captain of yours is an awfully imposing man for being so much younger than me.

53
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:57,640
It's kind of irritating. Still, for all his growling, he's not a bad guy.

54
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,140
Yeah.

55
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:00,220
Okay, go on and have a seat.

56
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:00,760
Yes, sir!

57
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:04,240
Now, let's see here.

58
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:14,460
Water recovery magic. Koala operation.

59
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:19,020
Wow, look at that. They got you pretty good, but don't worry.

60
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:26,860
My spell sees through the body of a person it envelops, so I can zero in on the affected areas and heal them with extreme precision.

61
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:32,020
Yami's no slouch, but you've got some pretty amazing muscles there yourself.

62
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,620
Thanks, I train hard.

63
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,400
And now for some mana to help with the healing.

64
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:44,580
I thought I was never going to get out of there.

65
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:49,660
Now that the Golden Dawn's five jillion prisoners have been transported, I can track down Asta and go.

66
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:52,460
Whoa! What the heck is that?

67
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:54,780
Some kind of jellyfish healing spell?

68
00:05:54,780 --> 00:06:02,640
Asta.

69
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,180
Hmm?

70
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:30,500
Oh, sorry, Finral. Have you been waiting long?

71
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:35,400
It's fine, Asta. Don't worry about me. It's not like we could go before Yami's back anyway.

72
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:35,920
Yo!

73
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:39,760
Wow.

74
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:40,800
You cleaned up.

75
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:44,380
Yep, I knew it was my lucky day today.

76
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,500
Um, what do you have in the sack?

77
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,240
Um, what do you have in the sack?

78
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,400
Less talking and more portaling.

79
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:52,320
Yes, sir.

80
00:06:52,320 --> 00:07:03,460
Okay, listen up.

81
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:09,220
Some of you might have noticed, we've racked up so many stars lately that we've actually made it out of the hole.

82
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,620
Which is all thanks to you knuckleheads and the hard work you've been doing.

83
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:15,640
And so...

84
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:19,640
That's right, it's meat time!

85
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:22,980
Wow!

86
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:24,500
Yeah!

87
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:28,100
This meat! This meat! That meat! All of me!

88
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:28,900
Daisy!

89
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:29,340
Wow!

90
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,040
So yummy!

91
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:37,760
This is a freaking holiday!

92
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:41,720
If Yami's treating us, I'm going to eat a whole lifetime's worth of meat!

93
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:46,720
Marie, I would never allow you to eat such inferior food.

94
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:51,720
You want to cook a cut of meat like this to between 130 and 140 degrees.

95
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:55,720
We need a high enough temperature to make sure any nasty bacteria are killed,

96
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:58,720
so it'll be safe to eat, but not so high that the meat gets tough.

97
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,720
Say, ah!

98
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,720
So good!

99
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,720
Hey, Magna!

100
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,720
Wanna fight to death for this hunk of meat?

101
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,720
No, I don't!

102
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:18,720
Aw, you're no fun!

103
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,720
Got something to wash it down with, too!

104
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,720
I love today!

105
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,720
Hot! Hot! It's so hot!

106
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:29,720
Oh, jeez!

107
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:35,720
Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh! Please watch me! It's embarrassing!

108
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:45,720
So, I guess, it must be hard to eat with those arms.

109
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:50,720
If you need somebody to feed you, I suppose I would be willing to help. Just this once.

110
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:54,720
Hey, look! I can eat with my feet now! Pretty cool, huh?

111
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:57,720
Oh, they're coming up!

112
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,720
All right, Finral, show us the trick.

113
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:05,720
Oh, um, sure. Right.

114
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,720
Watch! The self-punch!

115
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,720
All right, you're next, Charmy.

116
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:14,720
My trick instantly disappears in me!

117
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,720
Um, um...

118
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,720
All you did was eat it. That's cheating.

119
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:24,720
Let's see it, Gray. You're up!

120
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,720
Oh, no! Don't make me! Please!

121
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:29,720
Shut up and do it!

122
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,720
Ah!

123
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,720
Here goes...

124
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:39,720
Come on! This is your usual guy!

125
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:50,720
Here's my trick! The Crackling Magnet Typhoon!

126
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,720
Light on!

127
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,720
Read, shoot, take off!

128
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,720
Oh, I can do some weight training!

129
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,720
That's not a special trick!

130
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:04,720
Well, guys, I'm actually feeling pretty beat.

131
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:07,720
I think I'm just gonna call it a day.

132
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,720
Okay, get some shut-eye, Rasta.

133
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,720
Great job, everybody!

134
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:14,720
Night!

135
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,720
Does Rasta seem a little bit off to you at all?

136
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,720
You're right.

137
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:24,720
I don't know if I've ever seen him go to bed early before.

138
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:27,720
He always seems so happy,

139
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:30,720
but it felt like he was faking it today.

140
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,720
I could see if a drink would cheer him up.

141
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,720
Maybe all he needs is a good death match.

142
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:41,720
Obviously, the problem is he didn't eat enough meat!

143
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:43,720
I wonder if something happened.

144
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:46,720
Ah! Forget I said anything!

145
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,720
Mary!

146
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:48,720
Mary!

147
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,720
So, um, listen.

148
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,720
Hmm?

149
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,720
I overheard something while Asta was being healed.

150
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:55,720
His arms... they're...

151
00:10:55,720 --> 00:11:07,720
They're never going to get better.

152
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:09,720
What?

153
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,720
No way.

154
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:12,720
That can't be right.

155
00:11:13,720 --> 00:11:14,720
What?

156
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,720
No way.

157
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,720
That can't be right.

158
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:25,720
Asta, I believe you were hit with ancient hex magic.

159
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:29,720
On top of that, your bones have basically disintegrated.

160
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:33,720
I'm afraid not even my magic will be able to heal you.

161
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,720
A curse.

162
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:44,720
You have my gratitude for summoning me, human.

163
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:50,720
If the best recovery mage in the kingdom says that's what happened, it's most likely true.

164
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,720
It can't be...

165
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,720
I thought that I'd found...

166
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:01,720
Somebody I could fight with.

167
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,720
No, I can't believe it.

168
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:07,720
He has no magic, and now...

169
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:10,720
Now he can't even use his only weapon anymore.

170
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,720
Oh no!

171
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,720
So...

172
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:14,720
Sad!

173
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,720
Asta...

174
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:32,720
I'm sorry to tell you this, but you'll never wield a sword again.

175
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:49,720
You'll never wield a sword again.

176
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,720
What now?

177
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,720
Like I'm gonna give up!

178
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,720
Huh?

179
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:08,720
You got me again, Fate, you big jerk!

180
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,720
But all you did was get me even more fired up!

181
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:15,720
I'm gonna find a cure for my arms somehow, do you hear me?!

182
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,720
And if that's not possible, then I'll just figure out a way to fight without them!

183
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,720
Without them!

184
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:30,720
These chains can measure the magic power of anyone they come in contact with, and you have none!

185
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:35,720
No matter how hard I push myself, I'll never be able to use magic.

186
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,720
You might as well give it all up right now!

187
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,720
You were born a loser, you worthless runt!

188
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,720
So...

189
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:45,720
I might as well give...

190
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:50,720
I almost gave up that time, but it's never happening again!

191
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,720
Just you wait and see!

192
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,720
He's fine.

193
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,720
Yeah, kid, you tell him.

194
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,720
Doesn't get much manlier than that!

195
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:02,720
Yup, that's our Asta!

196
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:04,720
Sure is.

197
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,720
I'll share my dessert with him later!

198
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,720
After all that's happened, he's still so hopeful!

199
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,720
He is pretty tough.

200
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:16,720
I won't let him near Marie, but I will give him that much.

201
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,720
That's right, kiddo.

202
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:20,720
Don't you give up.

203
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,720
I just might know a place where we can find magic that'll help you.

204
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,720
Morning, everybody!

205
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:25,720
Huh?

206
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:44,720
There's always someone around making noise or causing trouble. The hideout feels totally deserted.

207
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,720
Did the others already head out somewhere?

208
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:49,720
It's me.

209
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,720
Maybe they're still sleeping?

210
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,720
Things did get pretty crazy yesterday.

211
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,720
I can feel that key!

212
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,720
If you wanna hide from me, you'll have to do better than that!

213
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,720
It's Noelle and Finral.

214
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,720
What are they up to?

215
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,720
Okay, I think that's just about everybody now.

216
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:12,720
Did you hear them all trying to be sneaky?

217
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:14,720
I forgot I had an important errand to run!

218
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:17,720
Oh, I promised my cousin I would visit her today.

219
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:21,720
Like, it isn't totally obvious they're running off to find a cure for Asta.

220
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,720
Huh?

221
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:27,720
I guess since they aren't going on missions, they don't want Yami to find out and get mad.

222
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:33,720
Plus, you know if Asta found out, he'd tell everybody to focus on their magic night duties and not worry about him.

223
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:51,720
Looks like a place where you could find some real trouble.

224
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,720
You getting scared on me, Magna?

225
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:56,720
Yeah, right! If anything, I'm even more excited than I was before!

226
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,720
Magna and Luck are dungeon hunting in the wastelands of the Forsaken Realm.

227
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,720
Hang in there, Asta!

228
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:06,720
Gosh and Gordon are researching hexes in the Royal Library.

229
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,720
Hey, less creepy mumbling and more searching.

230
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:23,720
How to become a brother loved by his sister when hundred hexes? Hurry!

231
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,720
Hurry!

232
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,720
Alright, fine, this one.

233
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:35,720
Marie would probably be sad if I weren't able to heal him.

234
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:40,720
If Gaush has to know about somebody other than his sister, I'm wondering how to get serious, too.

235
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:48,720
Charmy and Gray are off looking for new ingredients that might be effective against curses.

236
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:54,720
Just wait, Asta! We'll bring back delicious goodies that will not only cure your curse, but will fill your tummy, too!

237
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:59,720
I've never seen that before, but it smells so yummy! Maybe just a little dazed?

238
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,720
No, I have to be strong for Asta!

239
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,720
Yeah! Yeah!

240
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,720
Yeah!

241
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:09,720
Woo!

242
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:10,720
Caught creation magic!

243
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:12,720
Now she bombs it!

244
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:18,720
We did it!

245
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,720
Let's keep going!

246
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:21,720
Yeah!

247
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:30,720
Hard to believe a squad full of misfits and troublemakers would be willing to work so hard, and all for one newbie.

248
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:36,720
I know. Especially considering that he's an idiotic, reckless, vulgar commoner without any magic.

249
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:44,720
Stop trying so hard, it's almost getting painful to watch. You're just a grubby little gutter rat who's way out of his depths.

250
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:53,720
Him, the Wizard King? Talk about delusions of grandeur! You might as well give it all up right now! You are born a loser, you worthless grunt!

251
